@display("std/docs")
docs: part {
  | How the docs generator is configured and what it's given to render: its styling, the
  | layout each section uses, the components each slot shows, the modules that render kinds,
  | the [lenses](#tools.docs.lenses.lens_kind) a site is read through, and the [authored pages](#language.markup.authored_pages.authored_page) written for its readers. A
  | tree enters its export once, as `docs { … }`.
  |
  | Its surface is declared in `std/docs/package.heron`, whose types the API
  | reference renders; each export is specified where its behaviour is:
  |
  | | Export                                                      | Specified in                                       |
  | | ----------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
  | | `site`, `docs`, `layout`, `slot`                            | [the docs generator](#tools.docs.extending)        |
  | | `lens`, `LensNav`, `LensFormat`                             | [lenses](#tools.docs.lenses)                       |
  | | `user`, `developer`, `explore`, `agent`                     | [the standard lenses](#tools.docs.standard_lenses) |
  | | `authored`, `guide`, `howto`, `step`, `concept`, `tutorial` | [authored pages](#language.markup.authored_pages)  |
  | | `renderers` modules                                         | [renderers](#tools.docs.renderers)                 |

  standard_lenses_in_std: rule(system.checker) {
    must {{ resolve `user`, `developer`, `explore` and `agent` in a tree that imports `std/docs` as the lens nodes `std/docs` declares, unless the tree declares its own of that name }}
  }

  lens_mark_from_doc: rule(system.checker) {
    must {{ resolve `@lens` as `std/doc`'s annotation, whose names are references to `std/docs`'s lens nodes or a tree's own }}
    then {{ the annotation and the kind are both called `lens`, each declared once in its own package }}
  }
}
